    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d766">

                <pb facs="0823" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">574.D7/1613: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hsieh
                            Chieh-shih to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Changchun</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-23">April 23, 1932</date>.<lb/>[Received 5:10
                        a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Minister of Foreign Affairs at Changchun has the honor to inform that government
                    of state of Manchuria desires to adhere [to] International Radiotelegraph
                    Convention of Washington<anchor n="87" xml:id="d766-f1"/> and general and
                    additional regulations annexed thereto. For participation in the expenses
                    International Bureau Manchuria requests assignment in 6th class. Please
                    telegraph date of notification of this adhesion to the contracting states
                    according to article 9 of this convention. Minister Foreign Affairs
                        Changchun.<anchor n="88" xml:id="d766-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d766-f1" n="87" xml:id="d766-f1-content">
                <p>Signed November 25, 1927, <ref target="frus1927v01#pg_288"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1927, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 288</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d766-f2" n="88" xml:id="d766-f2-content">
                <p>In repeating this telegram to the Secretary of State at Geneva, the Department’s
                    telegram No. 58, April 25, 7 p.m., stated that “The Manchurian regime has not
                    been recognized by any party to the convention” and that the telegram from
                    Changchun was being filed without reply.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
